import type { StoreItem } from '../economy.ts';

/**
 * The crate pool: four hundred items nobody can buy.
 *
 * A hundred sets, each one a jersey, an accessory, a clothing piece and an
 * emote at a shared rarity, is the table this was specified as — so it is kept
 * as four parallel lists in set order rather than being flattened. Set 062 is
 * the same set whichever crate you opened it out of, which is what makes the
 * pool feel like one collection instead of four unrelated ones.
 *
 * Every item here is `crateOnly`, which keeps all four hundred off the shop
 * shelves and out of the free starter unlocks. They are pulls, not stock; the
 * only way to hold one is to open the crate it lives in.
 *
 * Ids follow the renderer's second-segment convention (`cloth-hoodie-lb-040`,
 * `acc-chain-lb-038`) so a pulled hoodie hangs like a hoodie and a pulled
 * chain swings at the neck without a lookup table. Emote ids carry a slug of
 * their own name for the same reason: the pose is chosen off the name, so
 * `emote-lb-071-galaxy-dance` dances.
 */

